# The build context.
#
# Without this file, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile sends EVERYTHING to the
# daemon: node_modules (hundreds of megabytes), the compiled output, the
# local .env with the stack's secrets, and the git history. The image build
# then spends longer moving files than compiling TypeScript, and the local
# secrets are shipped into a build context that may be cached.
node_modules
dist
coverage
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.local
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
postman/newman-*.json
